# Generated from: specs/245-accept-rest-dependency-repository-objects/requirements.md
Feature: Accept REST dependency repository objects
  Official blocked-by records previously failed closed as
  dependency_dangling when GitHub REST returned repository as
  an object with full_name and no nameWithOwner. This was fixed
  by normalizing repository identity to a string before comparison.

  # --- Bug Is Fixed ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: REST full_name repository objects are accepted
    Given a blocked-by record with a positive id and number
    And a valid open or closed state
    And repository.full_name matching the selected repository
    And a matching repository_url
    When readBlockedBy normalizes the record
    Then it returns the dependency
    And it does not raise dependency_dangling

  # --- Related Behavior Still Works ---

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: GraphQL nameWithOwner remains accepted
    Given a dependency record whose repository identity is repository.nameWithOwner
    When the record is normalized
    Then the matching selected repository is accepted

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: String repository and repository_url remain accepted
    Given a record with string repository equal to the selected repository
    And a separate record that has only a matching repository_url
    When each record is normalized
    Then the matching repository is accepted

  # --- Error Handling ---

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Cross-repository identities still fail closed
    Given a supported metadata shape that resolves to a repository other than the selected repository
    When the record is normalized as a dependency
    Then normalization fails with dependency_dangling
    And genuine missing targets still fail as dependency_dangling

  # --- Edge Cases ---

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Upgrade detection completes for REST expanded blockers
    Given valid official blocked-by edges whose REST payloads include repository.full_name
    When detectIssueDependencyUpgrade runs
    Then discovery completes
    And those targets are not reported as dangling

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Post-apply detection does not mark valid REST blockers dangling
    Given the upgrade helper has successfully added issue dependency edges
    And later blocked-by reads return REST repository objects for those edges
    When post-apply detection runs
    Then postDetectError.reasonCode is not dependency_dangling
